<title>USA: GTE Corp Q4 oper share rises.</title>
<headline>GTE Corp Q4 oper share rises.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Call Q4 mean estimate was $0.81 per share.</p>
<p>				 1996			1995</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $0.82		    $0.74</p>
<p> Oper net		     784			719</p>
<p> Revs			 5,751		    5,364</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	   963			972</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $2.88		    $2.61</p>
<p> Oper net		   2,798		    2,538</p>
<p> Revs			21,339		   19,957</p>
<p> Avg shrs		     969			970</p>
<p>(All data above millions except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1995 Q4 and full year oper nets exclude extraordinary charge of $4.83/shr, mostly from change in accounting.</p>
<p>Full-year 1996 and 1995 oper nets include $0.01/shr gain on sales of telephone properties.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
